ίν (present third-person singular). Tense interpretation and clause attachment require separate textual analysis.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["ἦν","ἐστίν","εϲτιν"],"id":"LEX-0003","lemma":"εἰμί","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"Definite article; inflection and syntactic function vary. Article presence and absence require contextual analysis.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["ὁ","τὸν","ἡ","τὸ","τῶν","τῇ"],"id":"LEX-0004","lemma":"ὁ","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"Word, discourse, account; used as a designation in this passage. Capitalization belongs to the digital edition.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["Λόγος"],"id":"LEX-0005","lemma":"λόγος","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"Coordinating conjunction, normally and here; discourse function must be assessed locally.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["καὶ"],"id":"LEX-0006","lemma":"καί","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"Preposition with the accusative here; relation or orientation toward. Do not substitute a theological paraphrase for a lexical account.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["πρὸς"],"id":"LEX-0007","lemma":"πρός","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"God or deity according to context; accusative and nominative forms here. Predicate syntax at 1:1 must be distinguished from lexical meaning. Bezae 1.03 preserves the contracted nomina sacra θν and θς; their assignment to this lemma is contextual and does not replace the source abbreviations.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["Θεόν","Θεὸς"],"id":"LEX-0008","lemma":"θεός","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"Demonstrative pronoun, nominative masculine singular; refers back within the preceding discourse.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["Οὗτος"],"id":"LEX-0009","lemma":"οὗτος","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"All; neuter plural here. Its syntactic relation to the verb should be stated separately from its semantic scope.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["πάντα"],"id":"LEX-0010","lemma":"πᾶς","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"Preposition, elided before a vowel; with genitive here, through. Retain source elision and apostrophe.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["δι’"],"id":"LEX-0011","lemma":"διά","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"Pronominal forms; genitive, dative, and accusative here. Referents require contextual resolution.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["αὐτοῦ","αὐτῷ","αὐτὸ"],"id":"LEX-0012","lemma":"αὐτός","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"Become, come into being, happen; aorist and perfect forms here. Clause attachment at 1:3–4 remains under review. Bezae 1.03 at John 1:3 n=8 transcribes ενεγετο. Its tentative assignment here treats the letters as a transposition by context; the transcription is retained unchanged and the interpretation requires review.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["ἐγένετο","γέγονεν"],"id":"LEX-0013","lemma":"γίνομαι","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"Apart from, without; governs a genitive expression here.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["χωρὶς"],"id":"LEX-0014","lemma":"χωρίς","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"Negative connective, not even or nor according to syntax; interacts with the following numeral.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["οὐδὲ"],"id":"LEX-0015","lemma":"οὐδέ","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"One; neuter singular here. Distinguish this numeral from the preposition ἐν despite accent-stripped search-key collision.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["ἕν"],"id":"LEX-0016","lemma":"εἷς","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"Relative pronoun, neuter singular here; its clause attachment requires review of punctuation and interpretation.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["ὃ"],"id":"LEX-0017","lemma":"ὅς","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"Life; nominative singular. The contextual sense requires discussion beyond a one-word gloss.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["ζωὴ"],"id":"LEX-0018","lemma":"ζωή","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"Light; neuter noun. Distinguish imagery, contextual reference, and lexical meaning.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["φῶς"],"id":"LEX-0019","lemma":"φῶς","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"Human being; genitive plural here. Translation choices depend on referential scope.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["ἀνθρώπων"],"id":"LEX-0020","lemma":"ἄνθρωπος","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"Darkness; dative and nominative singular here. Figurative interpretation is contextual.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["σκοτίᾳ","σκοτία"],"id":"LEX-0021","lemma":"σκοτία","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"Shine or appear; present active third-person singular, intransitive use here.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["φαίνει"],"id":"LEX-0022","lemma":"φαίνω","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"Negative particle; negates the finite verbal assertion here.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["οὐ"],"id":"LEX-0023","lemma":"οὐ","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"Seize, overtake, or grasp according to context; aorist active third-person singular. The rendering in 1:5 is disputed and needs sourced review.","evidence_scope":"N1904-DOSSANTOS JHN 1:1-5","forms":["κατέλαβεν"],"id":"LEX-0024","lemma":"καταλαμβάνω","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"},{"comment_en":"No one, nothing, according to gender and context; neuter singular οὐδέν here. The Sinaiticus transcription encodes ουδεν as the original reading in John 1:3 and ουδε εν in a correction labeled ca. The readings differ in their encoded letters as well as segmentation; do not describe this as spacing alone. No image-level intervention is inferred. Bezae 1.03 also segments ουδεν as one word at John 1:3 n=18. The letters were checked on folio 104v; the word division remains the transcribers’ analysis of scriptio continua.","evidence_scope":"SINAITICUS-ITSEE-V195 JHN 1:3 orig w9","forms":["οὐδέν"],"id":"LEX-0025","lemma":"οὐδείς","lexicographic_references":[],"review_status":"not_specialist_reviewed","status":"provisional"}],"limits":["Only two target readings visually checked; no claim that all 60 tokens are independently image-verified","Source word ενεγετο in John 1:3 is retained, not silently emended","Nomina sacra θν and θς are retained without unmarked expansion","Correction K at John 1:3 is not merged into the original projection","TEI altIdentifier type Tischendorf has lowercase d; not silently equated with the printed Greek apparatus D","No final editorial reading selected"]}
